lopment  and the formation of larger notions of  political community had at a time  because this is right on the eve of the  development of Hammurabi's kingdom and  the final creation of what becomes the  kingdom of babylon the unification of  all of southern mesopotamia into a  single political unit that it more or  less remains in and there are ups and  downs over time for the remainder of its  independent history  and the way in which the merchants and  other professionals in the cities help  to forge the state is ultimately as  important as the way in which the Kings  and other figures that we read about  much more prominently attempted to forge  those states on their own and so that we  can have questions I'll stop there
 

